- packages/core/components/workspace/workspace-app.tsx (hooks at top, GuestLike type, DemoDataBanner/LoadingState/ApiErrorState components)
- packages/core/components/workspace/workspace.css (+.gps-spin, +.gps-demo-banner)
- openspec/tasks-registry.md (added TASK-005b row)

Behavior:
- When the API is reachable and a session is logged in, the search and
  directory screens show real guest records from the seeded DB.
- When the API is unreachable (no session, dev without DB, network error),
  the screens fall back to the original mock GUESTS array with a visible
  'Demo Data' banner explaining how to load real data.
- Loading and error states are shown for the search and directory screens.
- Dashboard 'Total Guest Profiles' metric is wired to the real count via
  useGuestCount(); other dashboard metrics remain placeholder pending a
  future /api/stats endpoint.

Test results:
- 256 tests pass workspace-wide (was 227 — +29 new tests)
- typecheck: clean across all 4 packages
- Next.js production build: clean. All 17 routes + 6 API endpoints compile.

Per owner directive (2026-11-12): UI changes are surgical, no full
rewrite. Adapter pattern lets real Guest objects flow through the existing
component tree without touching the visual layout.
